00:55:18.660 --> 00:55:20.820
other situations,

00:55:20.820 --> 00:55:24.966
to be able to dream and
to continue their lives

00:55:24.966 --> 00:55:29.640
whatever situation or
adversity they may be facing.

00:55:29.640 --> 00:55:32.610
And so that became our primary goal,

00:55:32.610 --> 00:55:37.530
and we decided to partner

00:55:37.530 --> 00:55:40.260
with more organizations around the world

00:55:40.260 --> 00:55:45.260
that have the means to be able
to reach our target audience,

00:55:46.222 --> 00:55:47.617
and through the film,

00:55:47.617 --> 00:55:49.680
use the film as a tool

00:55:49.680 --> 00:55:51.750
to be able to inspire, educate,

00:55:51.750 --> 00:55:55.170
and empower more women and girls.

00:55:55.170 --> 00:55:57.846
We also suggest to any
partner organization

00:55:57.846 --> 00:56:01.770
that wants to use the
film to empower more girls

00:56:01.770 --> 00:56:04.050
to talk about their empowerment programs.

00:56:04.050 --> 00:56:06.150
Because as Rana said,

00:56:06.150 --> 00:56:09.540
we didn't really mention
We Love Reading in the film

00:56:09.540 --> 00:56:10.587
because it's Asmaa's story

00:56:10.587 --> 00:56:14.203
and Asmaa's story can inspire more people.

00:56:14.203 --> 00:56:17.670
If it takes another empowerment program

00:56:17.670 --> 00:56:22.670
to be that little push
that Rana is talking about,

00:56:23.130 --> 00:56:26.400
then so be it if that
will help and support

00:56:26.400 --> 00:56:28.740
and enable more Asmaa's in the world.

00:56:28.740 --> 00:56:31.950
So that's our impact
campaign with this film

00:56:31.950 --> 00:56:34.683
and it's moving along smoothly so far.

00:56:35.520 --> 00:56:36.622
- Alright, so as we end,

00:56:36.622 --> 00:56:39.961
I wanna ask if Asmaa wants
to share a final word.

00:56:39.961 --> 00:56:43.211
(Rana speaking Arabic)

00:56:58.936 --> 00:57:02.269
(Asmaa speaking Arabic)

00:58:18.830 --> 00:58:20.400
- So Asmaa was saying for the girl,

00:58:20.400 --> 00:58:22.260
I asked her about the girls
in the picture in the end

00:58:22.260 --> 00:58:23.550
when they were all together,

00:58:23.550 --> 00:58:25.830
like where does she
see them in the future?

00:58:25.830 --> 00:58:26.663
And she says,

00:58:26.663 --> 00:58:29.820
I tell them that if they believe something

00:58:29.820 --> 00:58:32.160
then it can happen if
they believe in it enough.

00:58:32.160 --> 00:58:33.603
And that if in order to achieve it,

00:58:33.603 --> 00:58:34.950
they have to believe

00:58:34.950 --> 00:58:37.710
and they have to work hard
enough for it and it will happen.

00:58:37.710 --> 00:58:40.440
And that she still is in
touch with these girls

00:58:40.440 --> 00:58:41.850
and she tells them,

00:58:41.850 --> 00:58:43.500
I don't have to be beside you.

00:58:43.500 --> 00:58:46.110
You need to learn to
depend on your own selves.

00:58:46.110 --> 00:58:47.937
Her last piece of advice,

00:58:47.937 --> 00:58:49.736
she's saying amongst you,

00:58:49.736 --> 00:58:53.220
either fathers and mothers
now or will be in the future,

00:58:53.220 --> 00:58:55.140
that listen to your girls.

00:58:55.140 --> 00:58:55.973
Believe in them,

00:58:55.973 --> 00:58:58.350
believe in their dreams and their ideas.

00:58:58.350 --> 00:59:00.960
Because even if they appear
to be simple or silly,

00:59:00.960 --> 00:59:02.760
they are important to them, to the girls.

00:59:02.760 --> 00:59:06.030
So listen to them, support them
because they are the future.

00:59:06.030 --> 00:59:07.255
And she says,

00:59:07.255 --> 00:59:09.540
these girls, their dreams will come true.

00:59:09.540 --> 00:59:11.820
Her daughter Tamara always dreamed

00:59:11.820 --> 00:59:13.200
of being in a forest among,

00:59:13.200 --> 00:59:14.033
a lot of trees.

00:59:14.033 --> 00:59:14.980
And you saw Zataari right?

00:59:14.980 --> 00:59:16.170
There were no trees

00:59:16.170 --> 00:59:18.330
and now she's in France
where there's a lot of trees.

00:59:18.330 --> 00:59:21.030
So her dream has come true in that sense

00:59:21.030 --> 00:59:23.100
and she thanks everybody as well.

00:59:23.100 --> 00:59:24.180
So over to you.

00:59:24.180 --> 00:59:26.970
- So we need to close.

00:59:26.970 --> 00:59:29.310
I want to thank you all
for being with us today.

00:59:29.310 --> 00:59:33.376
I want to thank Rana for
being with us in person.

00:59:33.376 --> 00:59:37.980
I want to thank Asmaa
for coming from Paris.

00:59:37.980 --> 00:59:40.710
I want to thank Alejandra
for coming from Barcelona,

00:59:40.710 --> 00:59:41.910
I believe,

00:59:41.910 --> 00:59:44.220
and I want to thank you for being with us.

00:59:44.220 --> 00:59:45.120
Also, of course,

00:59:45.120 --> 00:59:48.210
I want to thank the three
programs that made this possible:

00:59:48.210 --> 00:59:52.170
the Program on Refugees,
Forced Displacement,

00:59:52.170 --> 00:59:54.780
and Humanitarian
Responses at the MacMillan,

00:59:54.780 --> 00:59:57.000
the Program on Conflict,
Resilience, and Health

00:59:57.000 --> 00:59:59.010
at the MacMillan Center of Yale

00:59:59.010 --> 01:00:00.960
and the Program on Global Health Studies.

01:00:00.960 --> 01:00:05.910
So thank you very much and I
hope your journey continues.

01:00:05.910 --> 01:00:06.743
- Thank you.

01:00:06.743 --> 01:00:08.725
(everyone applauding)

